   "note": "The same trick two nibbles at a time. A bfloat carries seven mantissa bits, so 128..143 are exact and `0x4300 | v` is exactly `128 + v`. Two bfloat lanes fit in one 32-bit register, so one AND, one OR and one vector subtract serve two nibbles. The bfloat-to-float widening is a shift on this hardware. This is the form the advisor priced near 24 statements for eight nibbles; here it is measured rather than estimated.",
